From 4e99ba4fc6f9c469e5eb7a89c361b74883c9c605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kk <kaiwalyakhasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:59:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] staging: nanohub: the Nexus 5X sensor hub, data path only

Port of the bullhead 3.10 kernel's drivers/staging/nanohub (Google's
sensor hub driver: an STM32F411 on SPI running the nanohub firmware,
with every sensor of the phone behind it) to 6.12, for the Android
sensors HAL: /dev/nanohub (sensor events), /dev/nanohub_comms (app
messages) and read-only sysfs queries plus a reset.

Left out on purpose: the STM32 bootloader and the firmware/app download
and erase paths. Nothing in this driver can write the hub's flash.

Updated for 6.12: gpiod instead of gpio numbers (DT: hub-cs, nreset,
boot0, wakeup, irq1[, irq2]-gpios), wakeup_source instead of Android
wakelocks, a plain struct instead of an empty IIO device, sched_set_fifo,
ktime_get_boottime_ns, wait_queue_entry. The hub start-up (unmasking its
interrupt, up to ~10 s without an answer) moved from probe to the reader
thread so an unresponsive hub can't hold up the boot.
---
